# SABOTAGE: T163 / ADR-051 R5 — a capture without a `source_ref` is given a generated
# one instead of being refused. Every retry of such a capture then gets a fresh random
# key, so the dedup identity never matches and a retried job double-counts: the ledger
# still "works", it just stops being idempotent for any caller who forgot the ref.
#
# Flips the missing-ref refusal test. The key-derivation test stays green (the
# derivation itself is intact), so the red is the refusal, not the hashing.
# APP: demo
# TEST_FILES: test/usage_event_ledger_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a capture without a source_ref is refused, not given a random key
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/meter.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/meter.ex
index 18e36a3..7f35a62 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/meter.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/billing/meter.ex
@@ -135,7 +135,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Billing.Meter do
   defp fetch_source_ref(event) do
     case Map.get(event, :source_ref) do
       ref when is_binary(ref) and byte_size(ref) > 0 -> {:ok, ref}
-      _ -> {:error, :idempotency_ref_required}
+      # SABOTAGE (ADR-051 R5): a missing ref gets a generated one.
+      _ -> {:ok, Ecto.UUID.generate()}
     end
   end
 end
